  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform solid sphere of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> and radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is lying on a rough horizontal plane. A constant force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4&nbsp;</mn><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi></math> acts vertically downwards at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> such that the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>OP</mi></math> makes an angle of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>°</mo></math> with the horizontal as shown in the figure. The minimum value of the coefficient of friction <math><mi>μ</mi></math> so that sphere performs pure rolling, is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0096_115be50b632c.jpeg\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 152px;\" />"
